      "title": "Jamal Musiala dealing with neurological issue after collapsing in friendly",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/sports/football-news/jamal-musiala-dealing-with-neurological-issue-after-collapsing-in-friendly-126081900220_1.html",
      "description": "Bayern Munich midfielder Jamal Musiala said he's dealing with a neurological issue but doing well despite collapsing during a preseason game Tuesday at Heidenheim, three days after a similar incident against Leipzig.\nThe 23-year-old Germany international went down shortly after entering Tuesday's friendly as a substitute in the second half. Players from both teams made a circle around Musiala as he received medical treatment. He was then helped as he walked off the pitch.\nMusiala had collapsed Saturday during a friendly against Leipzig. German news agency DPA reported he had left the field on his own but still appeared dazed.\nAfter Tuesday's game, Musiala posted a message on his Instagram account, explaining that he had been diagnosed with temporary \"but easily treatable absence seizures\" caused by a neurological problem.\n\"These can lead to the moments that happened recently, such as against Leipzig or even now in Heidenheim,\" Musiala wrote.\nBayern, in its report on Tuesday's game",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-19T04:23:28"
    }
